<div class="text guide-styles" data-units-dynamic="article" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">
<div class="markup-toc-wrapper">
<button class="markup-toc-button">Show Table of Contents</button></div>Welcome to Wowhead's Pre-Raid Best in Slot Gear list for Combat Rogue DPS in Cataclysm Classic Phase 3. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from dungeons, professions, Bind on Equip drops, reputations, justice points, and valor points.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">
<span class="c4">Pre-Raid Best in Slot Gear for Combat Rogue DPS Phase 3 Cataclysm</span></h2>A Combat Rogue's first priorities are meeting the expertise and hit caps of 6.5% and 8% respectively. Expertise will be a bit tricky depending on what gear you already have to work with. Hit, on the other hand, is made very easy to do thanks to our talent <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=13843/precision">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_marksmanship.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Precision</span></a>. Hit after the 8% cap is not a dead stat as it still continues to increase our poison hit chance up to the spell hit cap of 17% and auto attacks up to the hard cap of 27%, but reaching the poison hit cap is no longer a hard rule as it has been in the past. Hit's value remains above the other stats until you get closer to the spell hit cap. The theory behind this is that as you approach the spell hit cap, the likelihood of having <a class="q1 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=2892/deadly-poison">
<img alt="Deadly Poison" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_rogue_dualweild.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Deadly Poison</span></a> fall off is marginalized giving more weight to the other stats.<br/>
<br/>With the introduction of the reforging system, we will be able to take 40% of an unwanted or lesser valued stat and switch it over to a secondary stat that is not already present on the piece. As a  general rule, you'll aim to get your expertise cap and then make sure every piece has haste and mastery on it ideally by reforging off crit and hit.<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Hit Rating - As mentioned, you will need to reach your hit cap of 8% (2% after <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=13843/precision">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_marksmanship.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Precision</span></a>). This should be automatically met with excess with any decent set of gear. If you find yourself below this benchmark, simply look to reforge an item to hit or throw in a hit gem.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Expertise Rating - Expertise reduces the chance for our attacks to be dodged or parried. We will always want to hit this cap of 6.5% or 781 rating to ensure we're never missing any special attacks or autos.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Agility - Agility is the primary base stat for rogues, and is always good to get more of. We passively get 5% more of this stat in Cataclysm thanks to <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=86531/leather-specialization">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_leather_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leather Specialization</span></a>. Agility gives 2 attack power per point and a little bit of critical strike chance for your attacks.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Haste - This stat Indirectly increases our energy regeneration by causing us to attack faster which in turn triggers more <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=35546/combat-potency">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_shortblade_38.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Combat Potency</span></a> procs. Haste is also changed for Rogues and Druids causing it to directly increase our energy regeneration. This makes haste an extremely valuable stat for a Combat Rogue.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Critical Strike - This has the same effect it has always had in that it increases our critical strike chance doubling the amount of damage done when we do crit. Crit is an overall underwhelming stat for Rogues of all varieties in Cataclysm, with Combat being no exception.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Mastery - Mastery is an all new stat introduced in Cataclysm that has a unique effect based on whatever specialization you are playing. For Combat, the mastery is <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=76806/main-gauche">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_shortblade_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Main Gauche</span></a>. This effectively acts the same way as <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=13964/hack-and-slash">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_27.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Hack and Slash</span></a>, giving us an extra main hand attack when triggered. Based on current information, haste and mastery are always in a balancing act and they generally have equal value.</div></li></ol>
<div class="wh-center" style="text-align: -webkit-center;">
